.Dd September 28, 2026
.Dt MOUNT_GEFS 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm mount_gefs
.Nd mount a gefs file system, or one of its snapshots
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl o Ar options
.Ar special node
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
attaches a label of the gefs file system on the block device
.Ar special
to the directory
.Ar node .
A gefs file system holds several trees, each named by a label:
.Dq main
by default, forks (mutable copies) and snapshots (read-only).
The labels of one device may be mounted at the same time on different
nodes; they share one block cache and one set of kernel threads, and each
mount has its own device number, so files that a fork shares with its
base are not taken for hard links of each other.
A label is mounted at most once.
.Pp
The options are those of
.Xr mount 8
.Pq Cm ro , rw , update , noatime , nodev , nosuid , noexec , sync , async , force
and:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Cm snap= Ns Ar label
Mount
.Ar label
instead of
.Dq main .
A snapshot may only be mounted read-only.
The label
.Dq dump
(9front's view of all the snapshots) is not supported; mount the
snapshots themselves.
.It Cm cache= Ns Ar MiB
The size of the block cache, when this mount is the first of its device
(default 64).
.El
.Pp
Access times are updated at most once a day unless the file changed
since
.Pq Dq relatime ,
and reach the disk with the next commit that happens anyway.
.Sh POWER
gefs writes nothing while nothing changes: the syncer's periodic call
commits only when there are changes, file data goes into the tree when
its pages are written back, and one commit (two device cache flushes)
takes all of it.
An idle mount does no disk I/O at all; automatic snapshots are taken by
such commits and only for labels that changed.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Mount the file system, a fork of it for build output, and yesterday's
snapshot:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
mount -t gefs /dev/dk1 /
mount -t gefs -o snap=obj /dev/dk1 /usr/obj
mount -t gefs -o ro,snap=main@day.2026.09.27_00:00:00 /dev/dk1 /mnt
.Ed
.Pp
The
.Xr fstab 5
entries:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
NAME=gefsroot	/		gefs	rw		0 0
NAME=gefsroot	/usr/obj	gefs	rw,snap=obj	0 0
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr mount 2 ,
.Xr fstab 5 ,
.Xr gefs 8 ,
.Xr mount 8
.Sh HISTORY
gefs was written by Ori Bernstein for 9front.
The
.Nx
port appeared in 2026.
